comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-22T11:35:24.525Z",pi-agent,"Implemented the fleet's mandatory gates as the first sim-to-RL environment, to every acceptance criterion.\n\n- Gate-simulator environments: `pm rl episode env register` pins the repository commit, the mandatory gate command set, and the verdict extraction (rule all_exit_zero), registered as a content-addressed Environment item (SHA-256 of the canonical spec; id carries the hash prefix) and re-verified by re-hash on every episode read.\n- Candidate-tree identity: `pm rl episode record` stores a content-addressed identity for the judged artifact - a git tree id (--candidate-tree) or the SHA-256 of the producing patch (--patch-file) - refusing an episode that records neither (candidate_tree_unrecorded).\n- Exact replay: `pm rl episode replay <id>` resolves the recorded artifact FIRST (mismatch refused: candidate_tree_mismatch / candidate_patch_mismatch / candidate_tree_unresolved), then re-derives the verdict from fresh gate results under the pinned extraction; a changed verdict is refused naming every gate whose exit moved (verdict_changed). Replay never mutates the episode (asserted byte-for-byte in tests).\n- Pull-request linkage and paired-cohort gap: every episode requires a stable --pull-request link; `pm rl outcome record` records real merge outcomes content-addressed by (link, merged); `pm rl simreal gap` pairs by link and reports sandbox gate-pass rate (per EPISODE) against real merge rate (per DISTINCT pull request) with both denominators stated; unpaired episodes/outcomes are reported separately as coverage counts and never folded into a rate. Contradictory outcomes are refused (outcome_conflict); unreadable corpus entries refuse the report rather than shrinking it (episode_unreadable / outcome_unreadable).\n- Credentials: episode pull-request links and patch contents are scanned and refused on GitHub tokens, fine-grained PATs, userinfo URLs, private keys, AWS key ids, and assigned secret literals (credential_detected).\n\nMeasured gates this session: npm test 203/203 pass; npm run coverage - 13 source file(s) at 100/100/100 lines/branches/functions, thresholds met; npm run docstring - 13 file(s), 101 declaration(s) documented; typecheck, lint, jscpd duplicates all green; ./.bin/pm health --strict-exit green (pinned binary).\n\nRevert-proof verification: 12 refusal paths were each temporarily reverted with the guard deleted or neutralized and their pinned test confirmed to FAIL, then restored from git: candidate_tree_unrecorded (record + replay), credential_detected, environment_was_mutated, environment_identity_collision, candidate_tree_mismatch/candidate_patch_mismatch/candidate_tree_unresolved, verdict_changed, unknown_gate_result/missing_gate_result, episode_identity_collision, outcome_identity_collision, outcome_conflict, episode_unreadable/outcome_unreadable.\n"
  "2026-08-24T08:53:29.422Z",pi-agent,"Review follow-up (PR 16 round 3): closure evidence now cites the exact regression tests in test/gatesim.test.ts that pin this feature behaviour. Candidate artifacts: an episode records the candidate tree identity, links the pull request, and derives the verdict from the pinned extraction; recording refuses an episode with neither a candidate tree nor a patch, and unknown or incomplete gate results; replay resolves the exact candidate artifact and reproduces the verdict without mutating the episode; replay refuses a foreign candidate tree, a foreign patch, and a changed verdict. Credentials: credential scanning refuses tokens, userinfo URLs, private keys and keyed secret literals, and passes ordinary diffs; recording refuses credentials in the pull request link or the patch content. Gate results and verdict extraction: gate environment parsing pins the commit, gate set and verdict extraction, and refuses everything else; verdict extraction follows the pinned rule over complete, known gate results; verdict extraction refuses an empty result set instead of vacuously passing; gate result parsing refuses a duplicated gate report. Identity collisions: episode registration is idempotent by full provenance and refuses a mutated environment; gate environment registration is idempotent and refuses identity collisions and unreadable environments; episodes and outcomes refuse identity collisions, and outcomes are idempotent and unreadable-proof. Unreadable corpus and contradictory outcomes: the gap refuses contradictory outcomes for one pull request and unreadable episodes; pure gap pairing refuses contradictory outcomes for one pull request. New this round: gate results canonicalize in byte order, independent of host locale - pins locale-independent ordering feeding the episode spec hash.\n\nProvenance for the health evidence recorded in history: the pinned binary used for pm health strict-exit is ./node_modules/.bin/pm, version 2026.8.20 (devDependency @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.20)."
close_reason: "All acceptance criteria implemented and tested: content-addressed gate environment pinning commit+gates+extraction; episodes store candidate-tree/patch identity and replay resolves that exact artifact before re-deriving the verdict; stable per-episode pull-request links; sim-to-real gap over the paired cohort with denominators stated and unpaired sides as coverage; credential capture refused at record time. Gates: 203/203 tests, coverage 100/100/100 (13 files), docstring 101 declarations, lint/duplicates/typecheck/pm-health green. 12 refusal paths verified revert-proof."
body: ""
